district we are in today could not be  here and i'm glad to be here  representing the entire board  i want to welcome you to the coven 19  testing site here at unlv  this is a collaborative effort to  partnership with clark county as i  mentioned  the clark county fire department umc  and the nevada national guard all of  these partners have been  tremendous in helping us make sure that  we  are getting as many people tested as  possible it's been an incredible  undertaking  and it couldn't have been possible  without literally thousands of people  who've  made this happen so i want to thank them  today we're going to hear from greg may  unlv emergency management coordinator  excuse me dr louis medina garcia umc  infectious disease physician  travis haldeman clark county fire  department engineer  and he's the on-site incident commander  overseeing this incredible  i also want to thank the members of the  media who are here today to spread the  word about getting tested  on clark county's response to making  sure that as many of our residents get  tested as possible  the partnership with the media has been  what has  really allowed us to get the word out  and has allowed us the opportunity to  get as many people tested in such an  organized fashion  as you've seen from so many of our  previous sites the organization  thanks to the nevada national guard and  so many others has been incredible  we've tested through this process one  hundred thirty three thousand  six hundred and fifty one uh residents  of our community  and a hundred and twenty a hundred and  twelve thousand of those were tested at  community sites just like this one  including 56 245 tests were conducted  right here on this site  as a drive through so as you know we've  been operating the drive-throughs which  have worked out very well  they have had some challenges not the  least of which is the extremely high  temperatures  so i want to particularly thank unlv the  administration for stepping up in a big  way  to help move us indoors so that we can  have a cool climate controlled  environment  for everybody to get tested safely  spaced out and efficiently  unlv from the moment this was raised  stepped up at the time  president miana picked took the call  immediately and stepped up in a big way  with her colleagues  here on campus to make sure that we can  make this happen  and again has been a real partner and  collaborator in this effort  testing as you know is the most critical  way that we can  monitor what's happening in our  community and how we get back to work  as quickly as possible and open things  up  as the tourism hub for the united states  and really globally  we need to be setting an example for the  world of how you do it the right way  and these testing sites in my view have  been a good example of that  so we're going to sort of hear from all  the speakers here today who've been part  of this effort  then travis is going to lead us on a  tour of this facility and answer any  questions you might have  in your effort to help us get out the  word so if i could bring to the podium  greg may  unlv emergency management coordinator  and thank you  for your effort greg  well good morning and thank you  commissioner appreciate everybody coming  out to take a look at the facility  i can say that without reservation the  unlv leadership  and university police services is  extremely proud to see this  come together in such a way we're very  appreciative  of the community partners that we've  been working with  clark county fire department umc the  national guard everybody has  really stepped up we've had some safety  concerns that needed to be addressed we  had to find a location that we could do  this  in a safe manner that we were able to  segregate  the students that are going to be  returning the campus in a couple of  weeks that they wouldn't be  intermingling in traffic we segregated  a portion of our parking uh just  dedicated to the test site and i just  couldn't be happier with the  cooperation that we've received from our  partners  every time that we had a question they  were there to  change make changes adjust and i'm just  really pleased to see this  finally come together and thanks for  coming out  i would just like to bring up dr luis  medina garcia to the podium thank you  good morning everyone i'm dr louis  median garcia infectious disease doctor  for umc  thank you for having me here today and  allow me to  thank everyone for the incredible  efforts in continuing these  testing sites that are critical to the  response of nevada against this virus  we have tested a huge amount of patients  as they were mentioning before  and that is really important to know  where we stand and know what we need to  do  to continue to improve this is a new  site  the weather is probably the most  important reason why we brought this  indoors  and we have made some changes to the  progress and the  process of taking the samples and our  incident commander will talk to us more  about that later  through these incredible collaborations  we've been able to continue to offer  these tests  and partner with the community that to  keep us safe  so i exhort you to continue  your efforts in wearing masks socially  distance  stay home if you're sick and seek care  when you feel ill a lot of people are  i think still a little worried about  picking up covet in the hospitals  we have made it as safe as possible  please don't delay medical care that is  necessary  continue your efforts and and thank you  so much for helping us control this  disease  now i would like to introduce travis  helderman the incident commander for  this site  thank you dr medina um i'd also like to  say thank you to the  umc staff that you see sitting at these  tables around here  they're the ones that register everyone  we get and check and make sure  verify all their information is correct  so patients can have access to their  test results  as soon as possible uh thank you greg  may  also sir for letting us move inside i  would be swept my butt off outside if it  wasn't for you guys  so we really appreciate you guys letting  us use this space  um being in a climate controlled  atmosphere obviously makes it a lot more  comfortable  for myself the other people working here  and also the public coming in to get a  test  i'd like to say thank you to  commissioner naft for coming out today  showing your support it's awesome you're  welcome here anytime  thank you to chief steinbeck at the  clark county fire department  for really stepping up to the plate and  doing our part to handle  the pandemic for southern nevada i'd  also like to say thank you to chief  samuels of the clark county office of  emergency management  uh getting us everything we need and  really handling anything we ask of you  it's been awesome you never say no  also like to say thank you to the nevada  national guard uh  everything you see here in this building  uh has been touched or put down  moved up and downstairs multiple times  by that national guard  they're really the manpower and  workforce that  is necessary for an operation like this  to take effect so thank you  thank you to the media for coming out  today without you guys we wouldn't be  able to get our message out to the  public we really appreciate you  and that message is this we're really  encouraging people the public to  self-schedule  appointments this will increase our  efficiency here is also and it will also  reduce  sorry reduce wait times uh when you come  here  that being said we're still taking  walk-up appointments um sorry  just walk-ups people without an  appointment on a first-come first-served  basis  uh those wait times will be a little bit  longer than if you were  [Music]  registered  i'm in a moment i will give you guys all  a tour of this site  uh we will uh talk about the whole  process start to finish  and then we've got some volunteers that  will do some self swabbing for you  before we do that i'd like to open it up  to any questions you might have  you guys being too nice  yes sir  okay folks i think what we're going to  do is we're going to crack all this down  so we have more  better visuals so give us a second to  get this out of the way if you want to  pull out your mic  and then we can follow him around on the  door and like i said we'll  break it

